WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.330
Good morning, everyone.

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:05.350
Hello.

3
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:06.190
Hi.

4
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:07.010
Hi.

5
00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.270
We are excited.

6
00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.090
Very excited.

7
00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:14.630
We are popping into your feeds today to give you a special top-of-the-year

8
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.050
Office Ladies announcement.

9
00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:21.930
As of today, Office Ladies has expanded to be a network.

10
00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.130
A network.

11
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.150
We're a network lady.

12
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.330
And we want to tell you about the first podcast joining the Office Ladies

13
00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:30.690
Network.

14
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.550
It is a podcast called The Lazy Genius with Kendra Adachi.

15
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.790
We are so thrilled to have Kendra join the Office Ladies Network.

16
00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.510
We wanted to share with you an

17
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:45.970
excerpt from her podcaSt. This week's episode is called Starting Fresh When You Can't Start Over.

18
00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.310
We hope that you'll give it a listen and love it as much as we do.

19
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.320
I think we need a fresh take on January energy.

20
00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:01.140
We need some new words when we feel this compulsion

21
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:01.900
to start over.

22
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.720
I shared some of these words last January, actually, and I need the reminder

23
00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.200
just as much as anyone.

24
00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.740
So we're going to look at those words again.

25
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:18.760
The first word that will help us start fresh instead of starting over is continue.

26
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.220
Continue.

27
00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.800
Instead of beginning, continue.

28
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.980
Everything you do builds on what has come before.

29
00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:31.180
You're living a beautiful, sometimes messy life, and it's a continuation.

30
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.440
January does not have to

31
00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.200
be a restart.

32
00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.240
It is not necessarily a new beginning.

33
00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.900
Now, energetically, there are some really helpful

34
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:46.100
things about those feelings of January, of the literal turning of the calendar, but that does not

35
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.340
require you to begin everything anew.

36
00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.120
In fact, you can't.

37
00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.280
That takes so much work.

38
00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.920
Instead, if you feel

39
00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:02.580
the pressure to begin something that does not truly align with what matters to you, simply continue.

40
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:08.440
Continue doing what you're doing, knowing that you're not failing anything by not starting over,

41
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.080
by not beginning again, just because it's January.

42
00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.200
Continue.

43
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.000
You're really smart.

44
00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:14.500
You're probably

45
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.260
already doing a lot of great things that don't need a reset.

46
00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:19.180
They don't even need tinkering with.

47
00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.280
Just continue.

48
00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:25.900
And the places that you know what matters and you know what works most of the time,

49
00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:26.880
continue.

50
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.220
The second word is tend.

51
00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:30.720
Don't fix.

52
00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:31.760
Tend.

53
00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.300
Now, don't get me wrong.

54
00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.080
There are things that

55
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:34.560
need fixing.

56
00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.580
They need to be taken apart and put back together.

57
00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.360
But usually that stuff like

58
00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:45.220
toilets or an Ikea closet that was not installed correctly, we fix things.

59
00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.840
We can't exactly fix life,

60
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.700
but we sure do try, don't we?

61
00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.780
We come at it like a certain part of our life is a problem to solve

62
00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:02.020
and to fix when really most of our lives need nurturing and tending.

63
00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.540
They need compassion alongside

64
00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.220
correcting.

65
00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:11.120
And when we compassionately correct one small thing at a time, that is tending.

66
00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:11.800
That's

67
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:18.900
looking at what's there with kind eyes, not going too fast and taking it one step at a time.

68
00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:19.540
That

69
00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:26.200
is so much more sustainable than continuously taking apart and putting back together all the systems and

70
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.780
processes and goals of your life.

71
00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.220
So think about where you feel the need to fix.

72
00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.140
And if instead you need

73
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.300
to tend, the third word is small.

74
00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.060
I love small things.

75
00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.780
I love small choices, small differences,

76
00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:47.840
small steps, small probleMs. That's why one of the 13 Lazy Genius principles is to start small.

77
00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:53.340
The smaller something is, the easier it is to solve, to tend to, to manage, to live with,

78
00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.240
to incorporate into your life on a regular basis.

79
00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.320
But January energy is big energy, right?

80
00:03:59.480 --> 00:03:59.900
It's big

81
00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.200
swings, big systems, big changes.

82
00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.960
And that's why we can't stick with anything.

83
00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.060
We're starting with big

84
00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.300
problems and big problems require big solutions.

85
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.100
I don't know about you, but I don't have room for

86
00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.280
big solutions right now.

87
00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:21.720
Life is beautifully unwieldy and inviting big systems or big goals or big solutions

88
00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.380
into that is almost impossible.

89
00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:28.580
And when those big things don't work and they won't, I want to start

90
00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:28.900
over.

91
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:35.040
I want to call them all again and get to try again so that what came before wasn't a failure.

92
00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:41.620
Instead, let's start small, like really, really embarrassingly small.

93
00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.600
I told a story in my first

94
00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.540
book, The Lazy Genius Way, about how I started small with yoga.

95
00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.120
I have terrible joints as well as

96
00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.780
like a lot of frantic mental energy.

97
00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.760
I call myself a caffeinated squirrel.

98
00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.540
And consequently, being a

99
00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:03.680
caffeinated squirrel with hips and knees that are basically made of glass, yoga is really good for

100
00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:03.900
me.

101
00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.720
It's good for my joints and for my brain.

102
00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:09.000
Well, years and years ago, I knew this and tried to

103
00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.780
incorporate more yoga into my life, but I could not make it work.

104
00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.300
I couldn't get it to stick.

105
00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.440
And I got so

106
00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.720
frustrated by that because it mattered to me.

107
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:22.280
Like it, it, yoga mattered to me for reasons that felt right

108
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.240
and good and aligned with tending to my body.

109
00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.080
But I just couldn't seem to get into a rhythm at all.

110
00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:30.820
And you know what I did?

111
00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.080
I just kept restarting.

112
00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.920
I kept restarting the commitment counter to zero

113
00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.260
over and over again.

114
00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.540
And that was also defeating.

115
00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.880
So I tried, I tried a new approach.

116
00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.760
I made doing yoga

117
00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.060
embarrassingly small.

118
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.700
I said that I would do one down dog a day.

119
00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.780
One down dog a day.

120
00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:53.680
If you're

121
00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:59.000
unfamiliar with yoga, that's basically like bending over once a day and sticking your butt in the air.

122
00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:03.560
Some might argue that's not even yoga, but it was so small, but I did it.

123
00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.720
I did this thing that

124
00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:06.520
mattered to me.

125
00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:11.800
And because it was so small and doable over time, I built on it.

126
00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:12.960
And hear me,

127
00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.620
when I say over time, I don't mean like days later, I'm pretty sure I did one down dog a day

128
00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:19.140
for weeks and weeks without much difference.

129
00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.840
Some of those days I would do like a full sun

130
00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:27.600
salutation, which still only takes like 60 seconds, but I didn't change what the daily habit was

131
00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.740
of one down dog a day for literal months.

132
00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.040
But guess what?

133
00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:33.720
I did yoga every day.

134
00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.480
It was so small

135
00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:41.740
that it became part of my life and my routine in a way that worked in a way that supported what

136
00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:42.140
mattered.

137
00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:47.620
So your third word is small, even embarrassingly small.

138
00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:50.120
Nothing is too small.

139
00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.020
Don't start over.

140
00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:55.440
Start fresh by starting small.

141
00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:02.640
I just love the way Kendra breaks it down.

142
00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:03.800
I just love it.

143
00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:04.460
I know.

144
00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:05.600
She's the beSt.

